## Features

## Bug fixes

- [#36](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/36) Release the metadata-fetch subscription when a signal is published, and link a value signal to a domain signal published after it, replacing the fetch retry, the publication deferral and the subscription hand-over of #16 and #19; fixes data that stopped after readers were recreated on the digiBOX, the T100 and the FusionLN.
- [#36](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/36) Run subscribe and unsubscribe requests in the order openDAQ makes them, and pass data to a reader only after the device acknowledges the latest subscribe, fixing a gap in the domain values when a reader subscribes again.
- [#36](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/36) Hold a subscribe until the device acknowledges the unsubscribe it is still running, fixing subscribes that the T100 dropped when a reader was recreated.
- [#36](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/36) Raise the core event of a local signal when its domain signal is linked after publication, so LT and native servers that forward the signal announce the link.
- [#36](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/36) Connect the streaming after its device has connected its handlers, and stop the streaming's I/O thread when the device is removed, fixing an abort when the last reference was released on that thread.
- [#36](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/36) Register LT server signals with ws-streaming on its I/O thread, and catch registration and subscription failures there instead of terminating the process.
- [#38](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/38) Read only the part of the device tree a core event names, on a thread of the LT server that holds none of the tree's locks, fixing deadlocks with threads that hold a component lock while they raise the event; value signals are announced again when their domain signal is registered, withdrawn or changed.
- [#35](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/35) Link a signal to its hidden domain signal through a `relatedSignals` entry of type `domain`, the LT streaming specification's relation type, fixing devices whose signals had no domain signal; type `time` is still accepted.
- [#35](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/35) Take a linear domain signal's rule start only from the openDAQ `interpretation`, not from the LT streaming specification's `linear.start`, which is the absolute value of the next sample, fixing doubled timestamps from devices that send it.
- [#16](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/16) Resolve hidden domain (time) signals referenced via the `relatedSignals` metadata element, fixing devices that connected successfully but delivered no data (signals had no domain signal).
- [#16](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/16) Retry initial metadata-fetch subscribes via a sweep timer, fixing signals that silently never appeared on devices that drop concurrent command-interface requests.
- [#16](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/16) Defer publishing a signal until its domain signal is published, so the domain link is not lost when metadata arrives out of order; signals whose domain signal never publishes are published without the link after a timeout, with a warning.
- [#18](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/18) Handle subscribe/unsubscribe requests on the I/O thread to avoid a data race on the signal map.
- [#18](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/18) Guard signal publication so exceptions can no longer escape into the Boost.Asio I/O thread and terminate the process.
- [#19](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/19) Hand the initial-fetch subscription over to an immediately subscribing application, fixing data that stopped on devices that reorder back-to-back unsubscribe/subscribe pairs.

## Documenation

## Misc

- [#36](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/36) Bump ws-streaming to v3.2.1, which sends each HTTP command-interface request once and one at a time with a bounded connect, and keeps announcing signals past a client whose write fails.
- [#35](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/35) Bump ws-streaming to v3.1.3, which takes a time signal's origin from `absoluteReference` (LT streaming specification) when the device sends no `origin`, and no longer reads the specification's `linear.start` as a rule start.
- [#16](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/16) Bump ws-streaming to v3.1.1, fixing warnings-as-errors builds (GCC `-Werror=reorder`, MSVC `/WX` C5038).

- [#1](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/1) Project initial version.
- [#2](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/2) Import files from openDAQ SDK
- [#8](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/8) Bumped to 4.0.0 — major version raised to reflect the module's move to a standalone release cycle, decoupled from openDAQ core versioning.
- [#25](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/25) Precompiled headers and unity builds through opendaq-cmake-utils v1.1.0.
- [#28](https://github.com/openDAQ/LTStreamingModulesModern/pull/28) Bump opendaq-cmake-utils to v1.1.1, fixing the aarch64 release build (GCC `-Werror=stringop-overflow` false positive in the `date` headers).
